---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy" crumbLabel="Privacy">
  <div class="page-head">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="lede">What we collect, why, and how long we keep it.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="flow">
    <h2>If you just look at events</h2>
    <p>
      We don't use analytics, tracking or adverts. We set one cookie only if you change your
      <a href="/settings">display settings</a>, so the site remembers them.
    </p>
    <h2>If you add an event</h2>
    <p>
      We keep your email address so we can tell you when your event is checked. We never show it on the site. We delete
      it 90 days after the event ends.
    </p>
    <h2>If you subscribe to emails</h2>
    <p>
      We keep your email address and your choices until you unsubscribe. Every email has a link to unsubscribe in one
      click. If you don't confirm your subscription within 7 days, we delete your email address.
    </p>
    <h2>If you sponsor calenda11y</h2>
    <p>
      Stripe handles your payment. We keep your name, email address and the details you choose to show on the sponsor
      page. We never see your card details.
    </p>
    <h2>Spam protection</h2>
    <p>
      Forms use Cloudflare Turnstile to check you're a person. It doesn't ask you to solve puzzles. Cloudflare may
      process your IP address to do this. We store a scrambled version of IP addresses for up to a day to limit spam.
    </p>
    <h2>Services we use</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Vercel hosts the website.</li>
      <li>Supabase stores the data.</li>
      <li>Resend sends emails.</li>
      <li>Stripe takes sponsorship payments.</li>
      <li>Cloudflare Turnstile protects forms from spam.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href="mailto:privacy@calenda11y.org">privacy@calenda11y.org</a> to ask about your data or to delete it.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
